        <p>The mins' meeting of the Liverpool district of the Lanashire Congregational Union was held at the St. Helens Congregational Church en Tuesday. Mr. E. Shorrock }woke, J P., of !Layton, presided, and, in welcoming the law number of delegates, said tney were very glad to be assembled In that old church, whose miniater, the Rev. J. Owilym Joned, and men,- born, were to be congratulated on its having been in existence for 200 years. Referring to the changes iu the istrict. he regretted that they had loot by removal the Rev.. Elwyn Thome., W. T. Boyce f Woolton i, and J. W. Johnstone illerklev-street. Liverpool They web coined the Revs. W.H. Witta (Forint"). NI. F. linvenizer (Hartington-road,Liverpooli,and W.PRiddell (Toxteth,. who bad taken op new pastorates. The financial report was very satisfactory for the distroct hail done better than last yea., rinnei•ing about £OO more income. The total oontributions received amounted to £329 Ur. and grant. to weak churobes had totalled £1 101. es against £OO3 lathe previous yesr. It wee decided at the beginning of the year to reduce the grants by 7! per COM, bat tbe income was no satisfactory that the com- mittee were •ble to lay the full smottoL The Rev. T. Dunlop, Bootle. au elected chairmen for the year; Mr. Shorruck Eccles, treasurer, and the 1ia...1. Yonne. Warrington, secretarr. Mr. Yonne said that was toe thirtieth yvar of his sec rrrrr yvhip, nod that was the loegeat 10. Lloyd William,, lianin 01 erv"i lay preacher. The Rev. A. J. Villa, of Oldham, secretary of the County Union. In his adiress,.sald thet the. average</p>
        <p>ennui to weak churches in the Liserpoo tic wet £.13 hitcher then in other Cleric's in the onion. Some</p>
        <p>churches in the district had been helped fcr a good many years, and he tbonght the time had come when they &amp;florid endeavour to reduce their demands, and xi I liberate the funds of the union for the purpoan of extending propatenda to those districts where Congre- gationalism was not now represented.</p>
