        <p>Runcorn have not come badly out of the Redone disturbance thereon January 21at, when the epectators mobbed Mr. T. 11. King, of Salford, and the Oldham players at the conclusion of the match. Briefly the findings of the committee afmr a long hearing on Thursday, were that the charges were correct, and they fined the -club 1.30, ordered them to pay the expenses of the incpiiry, to poet warning bills to pro- vide eufficient police to prevent the crowd from crossing the playing pitch at the conclueion of the match, end to provide dressieg accommodation for the referee, touch judges, and visiting teams Th. last I two were recommendations, but tie. Runcorn officials promised they should be carried out.</p>
