        <p>0 1 3 ..217 ..013 .. 0 0 0 ..000</p>
        <p>At Coventry, before 5,000 spectators. Widnes hegan the Booting with a try by Lally, which Jona Improved neon, and no crossed over leading by flee points to nil. Widnes added tries by McCarthy, Johnson, end Lawn, but kicked no more goals. Coventry obtained one try a Oldham. ;and were thoroughly baiten in both divisions. lteault :—Widnes 1 goal 4 tries (14 points), Coventry 1 try (3 points). RCNCCiRN BEATEN AT HOME. This match on the 1 rwell-lene ground with Stiford was not characterised by very good play, both teams giving • wretched exhibition for the greater part of the game. The Brat try was scored towards the end of the Itret moiety, when Curzon race; wed from Clarke and gut over, Lambert adding the extra points. Crossing over with • lead of five point. Salford were early on the agreesive. After good work by John, Moeda. and Boker the letter got over with • splendid try, W. Morass failing to improve. From • melee on the lino Walker just wriggled over, Shaw hitting the post. With five minutes to go Barker added another try with • aplendid indi•idusi effort, W. Thomas again minting, and in the lest minute Cooke scored a sensational try after brilliant play, Lambert adding the points. Result Salford, 2 goals 4 trim 16 (points); Runcorn, 1 try (3 points.) Teams and offizials : Eob4Orn—O. Shaw, back ; A. Hugh.. J. E. Steven. non, F. Steel, and R. Fl , three-cleaner bark.; C. White and S. Wootton, half backs; A. Peacock, J. Walker. H. Joyce, H. Chubb, R. ?lama, and R.Padhury, forwards. oSAlford—W. Lambert, back J. H. Cooke, W. loonies, biretta. and Barker, three-quarter becks ; E. C. May and W. D. John, half backs; D. Thom, R. /litchis, E. Rees, S. Warwick, E. Curzon and J. Memnon, forward. 11.1eree. MW. W. Taylor Mosta. Touch-judges Mem. B. Ball, Wipn, and E2Benoett, Liverpool.</p>
