        <p>WARRINGTON " A " Br. VT OLDHAM "A."—There wee a great game be •Nee. the second teams of Oldhem and Warrington at Wildempool on Saturday, and fully S,Ohn people watched the content. Fir). re-appeared in the ‘Varrington ranks Pfter three months absence end had n good reception. The •Isitore brought • very strong learn, including several men who ham done duty for the County. Warrington shirred in aggreasive style end forced Oldham back, hot Dixon clmred. Smart passing by the visitors gave McClean possession at the War- rington quarter, hot be tam grandly tackled by Clare. Some liege punting bv Mclntyre nullified the Oldtuarn attecke, and Warrington made headwey throngh a flee run to the line by Deintith, Fish claim- ing a try which was dierilluwed. Llewellyn end Tyson came awry finely, hut were bored into touch ley Fish. folotyre responded to the attack with a beautiful kiosk. Following up well he got possession again and peened to Clore, who raced over the line at the corner. Half- time, Warrlngtoe, I points ; Oldham, nil. In the second half tho Oldhern forwavde got tbe hall better then Warrington, end e hot attack was net up. In quick thecesmon Fish stopped Llewellyn and Tyson, whilst on the opposite wing Clare pulled tip McLean. The Oldham hack• again got going and McLean I equalised. Mclntyre retired hurt, Harmer going foil lack. After Clare had made • good rdn on the right, Fish received. ..I, easily beating Tyson end Dixon, made for the line, but wea hemmed In near the corner, and although surrounded by half-e-dozen Oldhamere, he managed to tend a long pane with a great effort to Boardman, who gave Werrington the lead. Before the BMWs Harmer dropped a goal. Final : Warrington _A," 1 goal 2 trim (8 point.) ; Oldhdm " A," I try (II points).</p>
