        <p>A year of steady commercial progress wan under review at the annual meeting of the Warrington Chamber of Conner. *high wan helJ at the Town Mall, on Monday morning. Mr. Oswald Lof.honee peasided and there wore also present (—Meerut R. T. Filmlough vicseprewident ,F. A. Frost, C. E. Barger, E. J. Hall, ll.Grosven-rr, IV. Jump (Ed. Gortor., Ltd.). 11. G. Roberts, Holman King, lon, J. Rymer Young I'. Brookre itaudley sod Alderman Bennett ,hon. secretary). lioitour Salmi, M.P., wrote stating that it was impossible for him to leave London, otherwise 'be would have welcomej the opportunity of meeting no important a gathering of IVarrington husinersinies. The M 1 rut, inn letter of apology for non-atten(l, anon, expreesed bin appreciation of toe good work the Chamber to.. doing for the Borungh. A letter wan also received from Mr. C.D. PA/Kit:MON (hon. auditor).</p>
