        <p>_ In connection with St. Paul's branch of the Church of England nien's society, the Rev. J. H. Bankes has continued his lectures on English Chui oh History dur- ing this month, sad the 'Gum-lance has been satisfac- tory. The discussions following the kettlrPli here been panel and bane ektended over fl itifil3 field of human Interest. These weekly or fortnightly meetings :says St. Paul's Parish Megrizinel, are supplying n went felt by intelligent men' who desire to know something of the history of the Church of England, and incidentally of their country. nod to In able to meet in srgument the better instructed members at other religious corn. munities. Moreover they are pleasant social meeting., and metre learning to know esch more intimately.</p>
