        <head>St. Paul's Church The Marriage Law.</head>
        <p>St. Paul's Church The Marriage Law.</p>
        <p>in the current issue of "Sr. Paul's Pariah Maga- zine" attention is drawn ton forthcoming sermon nt St. Paul's Church hy the He.. E. S. Dymort, vicar of St. Pridget's. Wavertree, Liverpool, co "The Marriage Law.' At present (the magazine states) the question of the alteration of the Law of Divorce is occupying avery prominent place in the popular mind, and we are awaiting with considerable anxiety the publication of the report of the Commission on Divorce, no that a sermon by one who bee made the whole subject his epecial study. and adds the experience of • pmetising solicitor to that an parish priest—Lir Mr. Dymott was a lawyer before he received holy orders—should be regarded as a feel-nimble opportunit y for learning something about this most important tab- JOOO. Our King lately reminded us that "The founda- tions of national glory are net in the homes of the people r they Will only remain onshaken while the family life of our race mid nation is strong, simple nod pure." It behoves in, all then to giro the most nerious coneideration to any proposed alteration in the Marriage law, and to make up our minds at to what is the duty of Christian men and women in this crisis.</p>
