        <p>The annual congregational tea party, concert and dance in connection with St. James Church, Latchford, were held in the schoolroom, on Mond., evening. There was an excellent attendance, over Sill) sitting lowa to tea. An enjoyable concert RAS given during the connect the evening, and the large audience fully appreciated theertorta of the various artistes who kindly gave their services. The Italien and gentlemen who I contributed to the programme were Madame. ' Fairhurst 'contralto', 'Miss Dora Millwood raccom- prinisV, Mr. E. Balrnford (WIWI), and Mr. Walter Moores (hrimotirist). Madame Fairhurst contributed several songs in a pleasing and tasteful manner and the audience ahowed their appreciation other talent by several encores. Mr. Moyers was successful with hi, rendering of several very amusing comic songa. whilst Mr. Ralmford allowed that he was a 'celloist of no mesa merit. Miss Lbaria Millwood carried out the duties of pianist in a painstaking and praiseworthy manner. i</p>
