        <p>• The members of the Latchfonl Itaptint Church choir held a social in the schoolroom on Monday evening, when two intereetingysreeentations were made —Mn. G. H. Heald, who toifere her recent marriage had been an active member of the choir for ten years, was the recipient of stoic, of silver fish bairn and forks. The presentation wns made on behalf of the choir members ny Mr. 1. Ford, the tre.ricer of the church. lit a Awn speech he referred to the excellent service rendered to the choir and .chapel by 3lre. Heald. She wan a valuable member, upon whose enthusiasm all , mould rely.—Later in the evening Mr. l'eter Ilerrieon, 1 who has been voluntary organist of the chapel for seven years, was presented with purse of gold. That purse area presented by Mr. Ford, nit., said be hoped Mr. Garrison would regard It as a token of the high esteem In which his labours on behalf of the church were held. His work for the chapel had been invalin able, end he hoped they would long continue to have the benefit of Mr. flarriaon's musical abilities. (Aptilausei.—Nle. Harrison briefly thanked the sub- scribers sod referred to the enthusiastic mariner in which the choir hail to,onded his effort.—Ao excellent , musical programed, was submitted.</p>
