        <p>and Ood teaonciling the world to himself through JCWIT Christ. There sees nothing more heautifid than that, nothing more loving or more green,tnn then the great King, longing with everlasting no for the nook of man, loan to him through an. There ron only one stipule, ion, and that en. that they abould believe. On Sunday neat, . will Le rean from our advert ire- meet column., ti..e pulpit at St..lnhti'll will be occupied by the Nloderetor of Manchester Presbytery, !he Rey. J. ff. C. Nlneaulay, M.A., .if Blackburn, winive power fill end eppropriete aermon on the occasion of the ripening end dedication of St. John's in May lust, appealed to all who bawd at,</p>
