      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-04_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>HOCKEY.</head>
        <p>HOCKEY.</p>
        <p>Latchford bed no difficulty in heating Wigan 'theme hut Saturday, he final ACOTN being Om. Wigan did not limed a strong team. Parker soon opened the ecoring and arising from great pressure on the •isitors goal grounds. and Starkey found the net before half time. Wigan did not put up much of a fight in the second half although their forwards made neveml threatening rashes and Travis (2) and Dale further increased the total. The visiting forwards wore easily held by the Latchford defence. Knight at left-half quite had up the Wigan right wing by sound hockey. Dale et outside-right made some excellent rune and centres. Wigan were best represented by their goal-keeper, centre-half and right fall-back, all of whom Flayed really well.</p>
        <p>Fieo-fibe Wigan First TIMM nppeared at Wigan on thesecond Eleven and so Latchford Second were not at their usual strength they were di.feated in an exci tint mime by 3.2. Wigan at one time were leading by three I goals bet Banks reduced this by nhooting two good goals for the visitors. It woo hard linen on tho visitors baying to tackle sock strong °await .. with a week team. Inlierwood St centre-halt nue %skit at left back played splendidly end had a lot to do with keeping the Wigan men from scoring more goals. The First Eleven v. Mead...ter l•niversity at Fellow. fold this afternoon is .—A Hill, goal ; P. Allanrion, T Dixon. back.; F Tole, J B Wilkinson, A Knight. halve.; K A Dole, Ii Parker, D Travis, C Hackney, E Blanks, forwards. Train from Central Station 1.22. p.m. The Second Eleven v. Manchester University "A " at home is ;—II Warburton, goal ; W T Kooks, A Waldo, hack.; Bradshaw, 1, Isherwood, It Parkin- non, halve. ; T Henke, .1 Pearson, A Starkey, W H Minards, H Fletcher, forwards. Bully-oa 2.45 p.m.</p>
