        <p>LIVING WITH SCARCELY ANY SLOOD. "One of my greatest troubles was breathlessness. My nerves were simply 'in shreds,' and several limes a day I turned faint. A doctor said there was hardly any blood in my body, but medicine seemed to do me no good, and I gut into a thoroughly low and depressed state. " One day a friend bought me a supply of Dr. WiNiams' Pink Pills. I had only taken a box or two when I began to fed more cheerful, and my appetite returned. Soon I was able to eat and enjoy substantial meals. Later my nerves became steadier ; I felt stronger, and the breathlessness left me. I kept on taking Dr. Williams Pink Pills and in time the headaches and fainting sensations passed away. I slept well at nights, and when I had finished a steady course of Dr. Williams' Pink Pills all Antemia and Debility had disappeared." . . . .</p>
