        <p>THE LIBEL ON THE KING.</p>
        <p>MALTA MARRIAGE SLANDER.</p>
        <p>A Year's Imprisonment for Mylius.</p>
        <p>For the publication of a libel on King George in print, culled the " Liberator," bleated Frederick Myliva won on Wednesday convicted at the Law Courts and oentencerl by the Lord Chief Justice to twelve months imprio,mutent- the maximum penalty. The 1ibe1...4A of the aonertion that the King had contracted a marriage with a daughter of Admiral Culme-Seymour at Malta. and bad subsequently bigamouoly married the present Q... Immediately after the sentence had teen pasted, Sir Rubel 1n.., theAttorney-General, who led for the Crown, rose and maid " I may mention now, my Lord, a matter which could not be mentioned until sentence had been panned. I holtl in my hand at this moment a document in the handwriting of his Majesty the King, and with your Lordship's permis- sion I will read it to the Court : I am authorised by his Majesty to state publicity that he was never married except. to the Quest, end that be marriage except with the ijosee : and further, that ho would have attended to give evideece to this effect had he not received ati•ice from the Lew (Meets of the Crown that it would I. MOOG. atitutional for him to do so. " That is signed, toy Lord, by the King himself," added Sir Rufus Isaacs.</p>
        <p>Evidence totally denying the story of the King's marriage in Malta was given by Admiral Seymour and several members of Me frmily, while the registers from the Island were produced, and they contained no mention of such a marriage. who conducted his own defence, did not crovs-exaniine any of the witnewee: lie demanded that the King should attend and deny on oath in the witnewchox the charge. On the Lord Chief Justice ruling that this request could not be complied with the aretimed declined to proceed further with los ease.</p>
