        <p>THE COST OF PAUPERS' MA INTENANCE, Th. Clerk suomitted reto•n of comovra•ive cost of relief for the year ending March 1910. The average !cost of maintenance for Runcorn Colon was Lid 11,64. —lnternee number of weekly indoor person. 120•15 at a mod of ss. o week. The average cost of outdoor relief was 29. 1•204. The totnl cost of outdoor and indoor maintenance per head of the population was 39.6 131. for Runcorn Cr,.. In other urban union, the cost of indoor and outeoor relief of the population varied from 39. 3d. per head in the 'Dwain I.IHIOD to 69.4 d. low heed in the Stafford Union. In the urban onion• the FOCI vnried from 12,1. lid, in the Suakin., Union to 5.. 3d. in the Stockport Coion. The cost in the rural onions varied from Its. 2d. in the Ellesmere Union to 69..,;2d. in the Kington . . .</p>
        <p>The Clerk said that this Linton compared very favour- ably with the whom of tbe unions in the dietrict of Mr. Duff, Local Government Inspector. The average vrorked reit at 4s. dd.</p>
