        <p>..„ ...... T'e fortnightly meeting of the Runcorn Bore! Council wise hold in the !Ward Room of Dutton Work- house on Tuesday aftwinoon, Mr. T. Wright presiding o•er a good attendance. The officers present were Messrs. G. F. Ashton (clerk), W. B. Hough (essistant Clerk), J. Farrington (inspector), J. Swinton and W. Dingle (surveyors), and Dr. Adams (medical °fluor of health,. LATCFIFORD FIRIDGE TO DE CLOSED. The Clerk read 'Plotter from Mr. H. Congreve, chief eosin., on the Nlanchester Ship Canal CO.. pointing out that a crack had occorved in the hydraulic cylinder to the centre press of the Knittsford-rond Swing Bridge which was pot in so recently an April last. A new cylinder of a much stronger type bad been ordered end SO remove the exiating cylinder end substitute the new one would again involve a temporary stoppage probably nbout seven days at the end of February and the Council were asked to consent to the stoppage. Consent wee given. WIDNES CONSERVATIVE CLUB. ANNUAL MEETING. - -</p>
        <p>...... There eel Only a sparse •ttenlance of the members it the Cu retire Club on Monday evening.—Mr. Crawford (chairmen) congratulated the merul,ers upor their success at the lam election inn it having any opporiition to their member, Colonel fl. Walker. Reviewing the political situation, he sold tnat the Government Were confronted with several vital iesnA, and upon the Veto and Home Rule hilla they could come to grief. He could not believe they could exist</p>
        <p>lor four O'r live years, as the Liberals thMght, because there were so many pitfalls in the Veto Bill. Even if they got this Bill through to their own satisfaction, they were face to face with a Home Rule Bill, and on this alone the elector. of the country would he very chary to accept such a scheme without a greet demon- stration.—Conmenting on the situation locally, ho said they must not run away with the idea dm the Liberals would not contest again. Ile anticipated that • strong candidate would be brought out against them, but on the other hand he assured them the their own orgenieeti on wee quite pretetred to meet them.—The Seurelary said they commenced the year with n credit balance of £5l, and they closed with It credit balance ol ,£llO, The total expenditure was £3ll, nod the receipts</p>
