      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-04_WidnesExaminer_art0134" n="art0134">
        <p>, desived from the concerts. more than repays the cost Aof on4.e.irition and also the fact that every additional subscriber materially helps forward the society's good worl, that many w.,u1.1 .6.cribe who do not . • ItOW do so.- .. The Society's next concert takes place on Wednee. • • ' day, February 15th and, as will he seen by an • ' tulvertisement in this issue, the plan of reserved seats *opened to-day to subscribers. 1 should be greatly obliged if you will help me to make it under- . Mood that anyone n..w willing to subarribe for the two remaining concerts, may cis so at two-thirds the .Wirbecription to the three, viz.: Reserved dress macs, 28.1 centre gallery (reserved), ss. Id.; side gallery and pecond reserved seats, 3s. 4d. So excellent a concert as that on the 17th inst. has</p>
        <p>noil teeny knowledge been previously given in Warrington. The principal works will be Beethoven's • nth Symphony and Tachgikowski's Piano concerto in B flat minor with Miss tom. Pierre as pianist and Mire 110• Amen as vocalist. Tim society'. fine •chorus will give a selection of choruses, including one by the -. society's conductor, Mr. F. 11. Crosaley. • Miss Pierce psi, pianist of ex..eptional power and ability,Miliß Arne!' is :dm a pleasing vocalist and the purely ortnestml work trill complete a programme It! unique in Warrington and all attending the concert will be both pleased and benefitted. Ateille Society's third concert Bei lioz " Faust " will be given in conidnction with the Warrington Male • Voice ChM, This concert will again be an excellent ,• one and it is hoped that as the result many will he tempted M become subscribers to the Society. In conclution I should like to say that the noel 'o committee argrand have been endeavouring to provide a reserve lona, the interest in whivh would render the society more independent and ensure auccessful working. Already £4OO is invested and if a consider- able number of additicnal subscribera could LAP enrolled and if a few friends of the society having the means would comet rwatil and help, an adequate fad could be quickly established and the society's position rendered double secure. -Yours, JOBS P. lEVICOLDS, hon. treasurer. MarlSeld, ;rappenh</p>
